  "notes": "10-segment, 9-point lathe: 140 triangles (the budget), one closed shell, no boolean.  The profile is a bowl, not a dome: inner floor at z=5 mm, inner rim at 11.5 mm, outer wall from 15 mm radius down to the base ring.  Scales are column displacements on rings A/B/C (10% / 12% / 8% out, 40% of that in on the columns between) with the raised columns staggered per row: two rows of five plates.  Materials by face centre: the inner dish (z>4 mm, r<12.2 mm) is wood_dark, the rim (z>10 mm) and the base skirt are shell, and the two outer-wall rows alternate wood / wood_dark per column.  The base ring stays round so the cup sits flat.",
